# Cohort operations — instructor control, never committed. The invite tooling
# and any roster (names + emails, personal data) stay local. invite_cohort.py
# already refuses a roster inside the repo; this is the belt to that braces.
scripts/invite_cohort.py
*roster*.csv
*cohort*.csv

# `bootcamp submit` writes here by default. Your submission belongs in your fork
# of the submissions repository, not in your clone of the course.
/submissions/

# Optional local graphify run. Not a course dependency.
graphify-out/

# The curriculum-entry workbook is generated and NOT committed. `--check` cannot
# verify a binary reliably — openpyxl may write byte-differently between versions —
# so a committed workbook could sit stale while CI stays green, which is the exact
# failure this repo spent two days removing elsewhere. The CSV it is built from IS
# committed and IS checked, so content drift is caught; regenerating the workbook is
# one command:  uv run --extra spreadsheet python scripts/dev3pack_entry.py --xlsx
docs/dev3pack/curriculum-entry.xlsx

# The rendered course site: generated from units/en/ and the toctree, and never
# committed. There is no honest --check for a tree of HTML, and a stale site that
# looks current is worse than no site. Rebuild it:
#   uv run --extra site python scripts/course_html.py
site/

# LibreOffice writes a lock file beside any spreadsheet it has open, and it
# carries the machine name and user of whoever opened it.
.~lock.*#
